.TH CCH 1 "2026-07-17" "codecommit-utils" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cch \- work with AWS CodeCommit repositories and pull requests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cch
.I command
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B cch
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cch
brings
.BR gh (1)-style
shorthand to AWS CodeCommit, replacing lengthy
.B aws codecommit
invocations with short commands grouped under
.B repo
and
.BR pr .
.PP
Every operation shells out to the AWS CLI, so
.B cch
uses whatever credentials and region the current profile provides. Repository
and pull request data are never cached.
.PP
Within a cloned CodeCommit repository the repository name is inferred from the
.B origin
remote, so
.B pr
subcommands need no repository argument. See
.B REPOSITORY INFERENCE
below.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS repo
.TP
.B repo list
List repository names on standard output, one per line.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-md
Write a
.B REPOS.md
file in the current directory listing each repository with its description,
instead of printing names. Repositories without a description are recorded as
"No description available". If the account has no repositories, no file is
written.
.RE
.TP
.BI "repo clone " name
Clone a repository over HTTPS. The clone URL is read from the repository
metadata; SSH and git-remote-codecommit URLs are not used.
.TP
.BI "repo create " name
Create an empty repository.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-clone
Clone the repository after creating it.
.TP
.B \-\-readme
Seed a
.BR README.md ,
commit and push it. Implies
.BR \-\-clone .
.RE
.TP
.BI "repo view " name
Print the repository metadata as JSON.
.SS pr
All
.B pr
subcommands accept
.BI \-\-repo " name"
anywhere in the argument list; see
.BR OPTIONS .
.TP
.B pr list
List pull requests in the current repository as columns of ID, TITLE, AUTHOR
and STATE. Titles and author names are truncated to fit. When nothing matches,
a message is printed on standard error and the exit status is still 0.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-state " state"
Filter by
.BR open ,
.BR closed ,
.B merged
or
.BR all .
The default is
.BR open .
.TP
.BI \-\-author " arn"
Filter by author ARN.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " n"
List at most
.I n
pull requests. The default is 30.
.RE
.TP
.BI "pr view " id
Print the pull request as JSON. Pull request IDs are unique across the account,
so the repository only affects error reporting.
.TP
.BI "pr checkout " id
Fetch the pull request source branch from
.B origin
and check it out.
.TP
.B pr create
Create a pull request and print its ID.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-title " title"
Title of the pull request. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-body " body"
Description of the pull request.
.TP
.BI \-\-base " branch"
Destination branch. Defaults to the repository default branch.
.TP
.BI \-\-head " branch"
Source branch. Defaults to the current branch.
.RE
.TP
.BI "pr merge " id
Merge a pull request. Prompts for confirmation unless
.B \-\-yes
is given; see
.BR CONFIRMATION .
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-squash
Merge by squash. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-fast\-forward
Merge by fast\-forward.
.TP
.B \-\-three\-way
Merge by three\-way merge.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Do not prompt for confirmation.
.RE
.TP
.BI "pr close " id
Close a pull request without merging it. Prompts for confirmation unless
.B \-\-yes
is given; see
.BR CONFIRMATION .
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-delete\-branch
Delete the source branch after closing. CodeCommit refuses to delete a default
branch.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Do not prompt for confirmation.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help and exit. Accepted by
.BR cch ,
by
.B repo
and
.BR pr ,
and by their subcommands, where it prints the help for the group.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " name"
Select a repository explicitly, overriding inference from the
.B origin
remote. Accepted anywhere in the argument list of any
.B pr
subcommand, which makes it usable outside a clone.
.SH REPOSITORY INFERENCE
Unless
.B \-\-repo
is given,
.B cch
derives the repository name from the
.B origin
remote of the current git repository. Three URL forms are recognised:
.PP
.RS
.nf
codecommit::\fIregion\fR://\fIrepo\fR
codecommit://\fIrepo\fR
https://git\-codecommit.\fIregion\fR.amazonaws.com/v1/repos/\fIrepo\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
The
.B ssh://
form of the last URL is recognised too, and an optional
.IB profile @
prefix on the git\-remote\-codecommit forms is ignored. Any other remote, or no
remote at all, is an error advising the use of
.BR "\-\-repo " name .
.SH PULL REQUEST STATES
CodeCommit tracks a pull request as only
.B OPEN
or
.BR CLOSED ,
and a closed pull request cannot be reopened.
.B cch
reports a third state,
.BR MERGED ,
which it derives from the merge metadata on the pull request targets: a pull
request that is closed and merged is reported as
.BR MERGED ,
one closed without merging as
.BR CLOSED .
This distinction exists only in
.BR cch ,
and is what makes
.B "pr list \-\-state merged"
differ from
.BR "pr list \-\-state closed" .
.SH CONFIRMATION
.B pr merge
and
.B pr close
are irreversible, so both summarise the pull request and prompt
.RB \(lq "Continue? [y/N]" \(rq
before acting. Only
.B y
or
.B yes
proceeds; anything else cancels.
.PP
Passing
.B \-\-yes
skips the prompt. When standard input is not a terminal and
.B \-\-yes
was not passed, the command refuses to act rather than guessing, which keeps
both operations safe to reach from scripts and CI.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AWS_PROFILE
The AWS profile whose credentials and region are used, as for the AWS CLI.
.TP
.B AWS_REGION
The AWS region to operate in, as for the AWS CLI.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B cch
exits 0 on success and 1 on error: an unknown command or option, a missing
required argument, a repository that could not be resolved, or a cancelled
confirmation. A search that matches no pull requests is not an error.
.PP
Failures reported by the AWS CLI or by
.BR git (1)
propagate their own exit status.
.SH EXAMPLES
List repositories in the current account and region:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cch repo list
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a repository, clone it, and seed it with a README:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cch repo create my\-repo \-\-readme
.fi
.RE
.PP
From inside a clone, open a pull request from the current branch onto the
default branch:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cch pr create \-\-title "Fix the parser" \-\-body "Closes the off\-by\-one."
.fi
.RE
.PP
Review what has been merged recently, then merge a pull request without being
prompted:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cch pr list \-\-state merged \-\-limit 10
cch pr merge 7 \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
Work with a repository from outside a clone:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cch pr list \-\-repo my\-repo
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ccclone (1),
.BR cclist (1),
.BR ccinit (1),
.BR aws (1),
.BR git (1)
.PP
